The '''Commonwealth of Cerdanya''' ({{langx|ca|Mancomunitat de Cerdanya}}, {{IPA|ca|məŋkumuniˈtad də səɾˈðaɲə|IPA}}) was a [[W:Deliberative assembly|deliberative assembly]] made up of the councillors of the four provinces of Cerdanya. Promoted in its final stages of gestation by the [[Junta of Merced]], it was strongly endorsed by popular consensus in May 1738.

The Commonwealth emerged following the [[Revolt of the Comuneros]] against the [[Nueva Planta decrees|centralizing ambitions]] Simmering unrest throughout the period led to the [[Merced Uprising]] of 1738 in Cerdanya, where colonial communities established the [[Junta of Merced]] to coordinate resistance against metropolitan interference. The Junta would operated independently throughout the remainder of the civil war period. Similar developments occurred in the [[Levante, Balisca|Levante]], where the [[Hesperian League]] expanded its influence, and in the [[Marañón basin|western territories]], where the [[United Provinces of Bayara|United Provinces of the Marañón]] emerged as a centralized political entity. 

Although it had only administrative functions and its powers did not go beyond those of the provincial councils, it had great symbolic and practical importance: it represented the first "independent" authority in the [[Baliscan archipelago]], and led to the emergence of a [[Cerdanya#Culture|Cerdanyan identity]] and desire for territorial unity.

